<title>SLOVENIA: Slovenia's Lek to list more shares.</title>
<headline>Slovenia's Lek to list more shares.</headline>
<dateline>LJUBLJANA 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Ljubljana bourse said on Friday drug company Lek would list another 1.7 million shares on the primary market taking its total to 1.79 million, or 92.7 percent, of the firm's equity.</p>
<p>The new shares, which were issued in 1994 and represent 90 percent of Lek's equity, will be listed on September 11 with a nominal value of 6,000 tolars.</p>
<p>Lek's current shares last traded on September 3, when they firmed 0.04 percent to 12,700 tolars. -- Marja Novak, Ljubljana newsroom, 386-61-125-8439</p>
